## Tuple variables with different types in the alternatives

```catala
declaration enumeration E:
  -- C content (integer, money)
  -- D content (money, integer)

declaration scope S:
  context e content E
  output o content integer

scope S:
  definition e equals C content (1, $2)
  definition o equals match e with pattern
    -- C content (x, y) or D content (x, y): x
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  The variable x has type money in pattern D but type integer in pattern C.
│
├─➤ tests/enum/bad/or_pattern_tuple_mismatch.catala_en:15.39-40:
│    │
│ 15 │     -- C content (x, y) or D content (x, y): x
│    │                                       ‾
├─ Tuple variables with different types in the alternatives
│
├─➤ tests/enum/bad/or_pattern_tuple_mismatch.catala_en:15.19-20:
│    │
│ 15 │     -- C content (x, y) or D content (x, y): x
│    │                   ‾
└─ Tuple variables with different types in the alternatives
#return code 123#
```
